## Key findings from digest
- Built: entities ENTITY_KINDS incl person; RELATION_KINDS proxy_for/member_of/overlaps (constitutive, never traversed, undated, ungraded); resolution cascade A alias/B ref_key/C label, D testimony; isEstablished A/B only -> persons mostly C. ENT-YYYY-NNNN 4-digit/year id (scale bound). entities R38 reportResolutionDefect (no UI). connections doc<->doc via one entity, bound 500/5000 pairs, 32 docs. corpus-export omits entities tables (corpus-export/index.mjs:73-112). Purge removes entities tables (record-core R72). No expunge (I-19 drafted).
- sources module: dated attributed disclosure history (pseudonym_link/attribute/name; how self/filing/third_party/hostile; knownTo), sources R6 identity claim without merge, R4/R5 known-not-recorded, sight list + read log; R9 rungs. No UI. Template for person facts.
- membership: members handle/cover, never legal name (MK 4.6); member_expertise declared vs confirmed, append-only; no conflict of interest/recusal anywhere (DR6 requires disclosure of relationships; UC-101 gap).
- staff_directory doctype keys entries by email, never name; meeting-minutes moved_by/seconded_by strings, attendance; DEC-5 office metadata authors (envelope extent designed not built D-124).
- Person-exclusions: actions R9 addressee never private individual (#namesPerson refuses person entity K707/K709); consequences R10 no person kind (code stricter); conformance act actor {role, body} never a person (conformance index.mjs:331); escalation R4 relies on actor-as-office; jurisdictions R24 counterparties offices; brand §5 / surfaceRules l.1711 "never name individual except in official role" (screen rule candidate conflict with K1452).
- Doctrine: no adversarial attribute/suspicion flag in subject registry (Case Making §4); no reputation/credence score (D-53; AUTHORITY-AND-TRUST); no centrality/connection-density ranking (PS VIOLATE 4; skills R17); machine-proposed look derived (D-82); machine may rule resolution (DEC-52/53) machine-attributed; entitycreate high friction DEC-88; Action §4 rule 10 no attribute of a person gates/filters/orders (members context); planning run reads no person's attributes (agent-worker R51); search not logged (OBS 4.6, DEC-68); D-15 / REC-36 candidate list withholds rows across project fence; entities instance-wide unfenced (OBS open ruling); DEC-78 sources rules (never first to make more public, hostile exposure as exposer's claim, consent); DEC-116 docket reply naming private person -> receipt only; DEC-11/DEC-5 surface all metadata (person patterns OK for public records); Intake 1a editorial restraint group policy; TAD store designed to mirror ("secret placed in it is published secret"); Intake 4a no restricted tier in replicating substrate; instance-setup R47 hosting account reads all.
- Real examples: Roadmap App A officials tenures approx (~2011-2014), resigned, recalled, CPA CFE, prior post (Houston whistleblower mgr->auditor), Audrey Lamb staff contact, unions; DEC-11 tracked change by named deputy; job applications batch; resume page class; Oakland PEC robots disallow (ethics corpus: Form 700 etc).
